{"name":"Innocence","hex":"#ebd1cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"innocence","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Absence of responsibility for a crime, tort, etc.","Lack of understanding about sensitive subjects such as sexuality and crime."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/innocence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Innocence","blocks":[{"text":"Innocence is a lack of guilt, with respect to any kind of crime, or wrongdoing. In a legal context, innocence is prior to the sense of legal guilt and is a primal emotion connected with the sense of self. It is often confused as being the opposite of the guilt of an individual, with respect to a crime. In other contexts, it is a lack of experience."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Prud%27hon%2C_Pierre_Paul_-_Venus_Bathing_or_Innocence_-_c._1810.JPG/330px-Prud%27hon%2C_Pierre_Paul_-_Venus_Bathing_or_Innocence_-_c._1810.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Innocence","wikidata":"Q359385"},{"title":"Innocence (2020 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Innocence is a 2020 South Korean legal drama film written and directed by Park Sang-hyun. The film stars Shin Hye-sun, Bae Jong-ok, and Huh Joon-ho. It follows a lawyer who defends her mother on trial for murder."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/06/Innocence_2020.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Innocence_(2020_film)","wikidata":"Q85972954"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Bouguereau-Linnocence.jpg/500px-Bouguereau-Linnocence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Bouguereau-Linnocence.jpg/500px-Bouguereau-Linnocence.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bouguereau's L'Innocence: Women, young children, and lambs are all symbols of innocence.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABouguereau-Linnocence.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Vieillard.jpg/500px-Vieillard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Vieillard.jpg/500px-Vieillard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Faience plate, Bordeaux, c. 1840, \"A shadow which will later become realized\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVieillard.jpg"}],"sounds":{"innocence":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f9/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-innocence.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f9/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-innocence.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-innocence.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f9/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-innocence.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-innocence.wav.ogg"}]}}}